Subject: Keep the decoder's work buffers inside its structs (the board's port)

The libmad that squeezelite-esp32 shipped as lib/libmad.a was built from a
copy that keeps main_data in struct mad_stream, and overlap, xr and tmp in
struct mad_frame, instead of malloc'ing main_data and overlap on the first
Layer III frame and putting xr (4.6 KB) and tmp on the stack. Its header
(components/codecs/inc/mad/mad.h) describes those structs, and the codecs
are built against that header, so building libmad from source has to match
it. This patch makes that change and nothing else; firmware/test's
`upstream` target (mad/layout.c) checks the structs against the header.

--- a/frame.c
+++ b/frame.c
@@ -94,7 +94,6 @@
 
   frame->options = 0;
 
-  frame->overlap = 0;
   mad_frame_mute(frame);
 }
 
@@ -106,10 +105,6 @@
 {
   mad_header_finish(&frame->header);
 
-  if (frame->overlap) {
-    free(frame->overlap);
-    frame->overlap = 0;
-  }
 }
 
